TIP:  The intro begins without chords (NC) but are followed by a three-note segment leading into the first (G).  So what you do is form (D) and sing the opening a capella.  Then after “closed” pluck the open 4th string <d>, add your pinky to the 4th string/4th fret <f#> and pick, and then sing “it’s” while picking the covered 3rd string.  In the second verse it’s just two notes followed by a strum of (D) on “so”.  If this is too much then just play the (D) in place of the notes.


